        "id": 3491318
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-01T01:57:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I based this on the `HTTP_LDAP` pattern, but I’m a bit hesitant about allowing a list of authentication methods. Each combination might need some extra research and work. Also, since `LDAP` and `OAUTH` can’t work together, I’m not really seeing a strong use case for having multiple auth methods here. Please let me know if you feel otherwise.",
      "parentUuid": "896ede3e_f987e131",
      "revId": "fe55c0b8fff3beb588182d67f48c24b4ec7eb0c8",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d11c0094_799f2e55",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 606,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-05T23:21:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about coding it up to work the way I describe (or even just using _ as a separator so it isn\u0027t really different configuration wise then what you got already), and then just creating a set of known good String combinations like: setof(\"HTTP_OAUTH\", \"HTTP_LDAP\") so that it can be easy in the future to enable other combos if someone is willing to test them out together?",
      "parentUuid": "9d58d249_d3b44c2b",
      "revId": "fe55c0b8fff3beb588182d67f48c24b4ec7eb0c8",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
